---
title: notes
summary: A plain-text Zettelkasten with a TSV query layer over the filesystem.
status: active
stack: bash, awk, fzf, ripgrep
repo: https://github.com/jplr/notes
---

The filesystem is the database. Folders are types, filenames encode dates,
frontmatter holds topics and people. A small bash CLI (`n`) reads that
structure and turns it into TSV: index, find, counts, cooccurrence, gaps,
orphans, walks. An fzf TUI sits on top.

No app. No sync service. No proprietary store. A vault of markdown files and
about a thousand lines of bash.
